  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Judicial Administration Reform in Ukraine (IDLO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will work on the eradication of an entrenched system of state-sponsored corruption and graft which was one of the core demands of the 2014 Revolution of Dignity, with the judiciary considered an enabling layer of this broader system. Local and national-level networks of oligarchic influence and control over the judiciary established since the fall of the Soviet Union have significantly undercut transparency and independence of judicial decisions, resulting in low levels of trust among Ukrainian citizens in their justice system, a general sense of impunity, and state capture. The legislative breakthrough presented by the adoption of draft laws 3711-D and 5068 provides a rare opportunity for an effective relaunch of the judicial reform with the most substantive concerns effectively addressed.

All activities and outputs delivered through this technical assistance project contribute to overall judicial reform and are ultimately intended to facilitate to the realization of the goal of strengthened transparency and accountability of Ukraine&#x2019;s judicial administration. 

IDLO anticipates that notable inroads towards the realization of the above goal will be made by resuming all judicial appointments in Ukraine in line with transparency and merit-based selection criteria, and by considering and deciding disciplinary complaints against sitting judges in a transparent way (Intermediate Outcomes 1 and 2).</narrative>
  </description>
